#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
A(Fe) of every selected Fe I / Fe II line of one star, for ONE fixed set of stellar parameters.

Run it as a plain script: edit the settings below, then `python find_stellar_parameters`.

What it does (one pass, nothing is iterated, so a run is fully set by the settings below):
  1. interpolates a MARCS atmosphere + Fe departure coefficients at (TEFF, LOGG, FEH) with
     interp_nlte_2.py; the departure coefficients are computed for A(Fe) = 7.45 + FEH (SOLAR_FE),
  2. fits A(Fe) line by line with fe_line_fit.fit_lines (see fe_line_fit.py for the method),
  3. writes the per-line table and a summary: mean A(Fe I), A(Fe II), their difference and the
     slopes of A(Fe I) against excitation potential and reduced EW, plus the REW slope of the Fe II lines alone
     and of Fe I + Fe II together (plain fit, no offset between the ions). These are for inspection only;
     nothing is adjusted.

Notes on lines go into data/selected_lines/<star>/fe_line_flags.yaml (next to the line CSV) as line_id: reason;
review_fits.py writes it, it can also be edited by hand. A flagged line is treated like every other line (quality
cuts, sigma clipping, means, slopes) and only marked: orange square in diagnostics.png, orange note in
overview.png, `flag` column in lines.csv. A reason that starts with "reject" (e.g. 'reject: bad atomic data')
leaves the line out of the means and slopes ("rejected: by hand (...)" in lines.csv). With ONLY_FLAGGED = True
only the lines in that file are fitted, e.g. to redo them with other FIT_SETTINGS.

Everything goes to  ~/NICO/runs/<star>/fe_abundance/T<teff>_g<logg>_v<vmic>_z<feh>_<NLTE|LTE>_<time>/ :
    lines.csv            one row per line (A, sigma, chi2_red, RV shift, broadening (broad_kms: the FWHM argument of faltbon,
                         see broad_profile), continuum, EP, EW, status,
                         NLTE levels used, and `selection`: used / sigma-clipped / flagged: ... / rejected: ...)
    summary.yaml         parameters, atmosphere files, means, slopes, which lines were used, sigma-clipped,
                         flagged or rejected (with the reason), settings
    nlte_levels.csv      NLTE runs: model-atom levels of every selected line (from the line list or assigned)
    fe_line_flags.yaml   copy of the flags used
    diagnostics.png      A(Fe) against EP, REW and wavelength
    overview.png         all line fits in one picture, numbered and coloured by selection
    lines/<line>/        fit.png and bestfit.csv per line (with the A(Fe) -/+ abund_band_offset syntheses as a shaded band
                         when abund_band is on); synth/ holds the synthetic spectrum of every trial
                         abundance (.spec from bsyn, .cvl after the instrumental profile) and chi2_curve.csv the
                         chi^2, RV shift, broadening and continuum fitted at each of them
    atm/                 the interpolated atmosphere and departure coefficients

run_point() does one parameter set, so a Teff/logg/vmic grid is a loop over it (see the end of main()).

AUTO_TUNE = True instead iterates the parameters (tune()), starting from TEFF / LOGG / VMIC / FEH:
    Teff    until slope(A(Fe I) vs EP) = 0             (excitation balance)
    vmic    until slope(A vs REW) = 0                  (Fe I only, or Fe I + Fe II: VMIC_SLOPE)
    logg    until A(Fe II) = A(Fe I)                   (ionisation balance)
    [Fe/H]  until the atmosphere's [Fe/H] = A(Fe I) - 7.45
Newton steps on these four conditions. The first Jacobian comes from one finite-difference run per parameter
(FD_STEP; [Fe/H] has none, its column starts at 0) or from an earlier tuning (JACOBIAN_FROM); after that every run
updates it (Broyden), so each iteration costs one full line fit. Parameters set False in TUNE stay at the values
above and their condition is dropped. Every run is an ordinary run directory in fe_abundance/ (name ends in
_tune<NN>), so review_fits.py and balmer_wings*.py see them as usual; the tuning itself goes to
    ~/NICO/runs/<star>/fe_tuning/<time>_<NLTE|LTE>/
        tune_log.csv     one row per run: parameters, A(Fe I/II), slopes, conditions, run directory
        tune.yaml        settings, how it ended, final and best parameter set, the Jacobian (per K / dex / km/s)
        tune.png         parameters and conditions (in units of their error) against run number
Nothing is written to stars.yaml; the result is printed at the end.
"""

